{{ collageFigure('/images/blog/johnny-castaway-moonlight.png', 'Johnny Castaway’s island under a moonlit night sky.', 'The browser restoration after dark.', 'Screenshot from johnny_web. Original Johnny Castaway artwork by Dynamix / Sierra On-Line.', 'red', '', true) }}
<p>Used in the <a href="/posts/20261019-johnny-castaway-browser/">Johnny Castaway post</a>. This example repeats crops from the main image.</p>
<h2>Use and reference</h2>
<p>Use once at a meaningful visual pause in a post. Keep ordinary screenshots, data diagrams, navigation and photographs intact when decorative fragments would interfere with their purpose. Both examples opt into restrained pointer parallax. The full image moves less than the fragments, while the caption stays still. Touch, reduced-motion and CSS-off views keep the static figure. The default component needs no JavaScript.</p>
<p>The supplied <a href="/images/blog/turbografx-16-advertisement-reference.png">TurboGrafx-16 advertisement</a> informs the composition; its publication, date and design credits remain unverified. Its artwork and branding are not used in the component. <a href="/style-guide/components/#cut-paper-collage">Copy the authoring pattern and review the component contract</a>.</p>
